WEBVTT

00:02.470 --> 00:04.940
Happy New Year.

00:05.430 --> 00:07.740
Happy New Year, Father.

00:08.310 --> 00:11.650
To another glorious year, Father.

00:12.210 --> 00:14.520
You look quite radiant today.

00:14.520 --> 00:17.120
To another glorious year.

00:17.370 --> 00:21.500
Indeed. I am glad to see that
you're all doing well.

00:22.410 --> 00:25.180
Oh, there's not enough sake.

00:25.180 --> 00:26.480
Allow me.

00:26.480 --> 00:29.740
Oh, no, Neko-san.
You're just getting over an illness.

00:29.740 --> 00:32.920
No, I'm quite all right now.

00:44.690 --> 00:47.860
Whee! Vroom!

00:50.370 --> 00:52.660
Oh, my. Are you all right?

00:52.660 --> 00:55.030
Hey! What do you think you're doing, Shouta?

00:55.030 --> 00:57.530
You need to behave today!

00:57.530 --> 00:59.030
Yuriko-neesan?

01:00.120 --> 01:02.790
Oh! Is that you, Neko-chan?

01:03.730 --> 01:06.650
What a surprise that was! 
You've gotten so pretty!

01:06.650 --> 01:09.400
I guess we haven't seen
each other since your wedding.

01:09.820 --> 01:14.260
Yes. I think you were about 
Shouta's age back then.

01:14.640 --> 01:17.440
Yes, I was quite small and round.

01:17.440 --> 01:20.820
Yes, exactly! It's so hard to picture that now!

01:22.200 --> 01:23.220
<i>Yes...</i>

03:00.030 --> 03:06.040
<b>#7 "There's No Point in This Confession"</b>

03:01.570 --> 03:03.490
You don't know what's causing it?

03:03.490 --> 03:06.540
Yes. It's not unreasonable to think that

03:06.540 --> 03:10.360
you've suddenly developed 
some sort of food allergy.

03:10.360 --> 03:16.250
But considering where your hives
appeared, that likelihood is low.

03:16.640 --> 03:17.750
I see.

03:18.220 --> 03:22.200
At your age, your hormones
can become a wreck at any time.

03:22.200 --> 03:26.520
It's not uncommon for even a 
little bit of stress to cause hives.

03:27.250 --> 03:29.320
A little bit of stress?

03:29.770 --> 03:33.290
Anyway, take it easy for a while,
and we'll keep an eye on this

03:33.290 --> 03:35.640
as we wait for your blood tests.

03:35.640 --> 03:36.970
Uh, okay.

03:37.550 --> 03:40.380
Please come see me again in a week.

03:40.380 --> 03:44.320
If anything else happens in that time,
we'll do a more thorough checkup.

03:44.320 --> 03:46.660
Okay. Thank you very much.

03:50.880 --> 03:52.920
Stress, huh?

04:05.220 --> 04:07.930
Aw, I should've gotten anmitsu.

04:07.930 --> 04:10.390
The ozouni looked good, too.

04:10.390 --> 04:11.040
Right?

04:11.040 --> 04:12.730
The first shrine visit of the year...

04:16.020 --> 04:18.360
The first shrine visit of the year...

04:18.360 --> 04:20.010
Did you go already, President?

04:20.010 --> 04:21.030
Nope.

04:21.480 --> 04:23.180
For the first three days of the year,

04:23.180 --> 04:26.490
we go to see relatives on 
both sides of my family.

04:26.490 --> 04:29.390
That's where I get to experience
the grueling activity of

04:29.390 --> 04:34.460
babysitting all the little brats under
the guise of "New Year's greetings."

04:34.800 --> 04:37.930
I've heard of people gaining
a little weight over New Year's,

04:37.930 --> 04:41.020
but I guess you get a diet
and a workout for yours.

04:41.560 --> 04:42.920
What about you, Kojuurou-kyun?

04:42.920 --> 04:45.800
I basically spent all my 
time in front of the TV.

04:45.800 --> 04:48.390
I binge-watched <i>The Solitary Gourmand</i>.

04:48.390 --> 04:52.350
Aw... We just rang in the new year,

04:52.350 --> 04:55.180
so I want to have some fun and 
celebrate with all of you guys.

04:55.180 --> 04:57.020
Like when we all went to the ocean?

04:57.320 --> 05:00.320
Hey, why don't we all do our 
first shrine visit together?

05:00.320 --> 05:01.000
Huh?

05:01.000 --> 05:02.400
Yeah, let's do it!

05:07.300 --> 05:09.580
Hey, isn't that...

05:14.160 --> 05:16.370
Messages

05:14.160 --> 05:16.370
Tae

05:14.160 --> 05:16.370
Edit

05:14.160 --> 05:16.370
Hey, look behind you!
At the café!

05:14.160 --> 05:16.370
Tae

05:15.200 --> 05:16.370
Behind me?

05:28.800 --> 05:31.920
<i>I thought it was up... but it was down.</i>

05:33.750 --> 05:35.020
<i>And then...</i>

05:35.020 --> 05:38.520
My stomach hurts so much,
I can't move

05:35.020 --> 05:38.520
There's a present for you downstairs
in my coat pocket

05:35.020 --> 05:41.020
Messages

05:35.020 --> 05:41.020
Makabe Masamune

05:35.020 --> 05:41.020
Edit

05:38.520 --> 05:41.020
There's a present for you downstairs
in my coat pocket

05:38.650 --> 05:41.020
Please just take that and
leave for today

05:41.020 --> 05:42.570
<b>I'm really sorry</b>

05:42.570 --> 05:45.240
<b>Also, Happy Birthday</b>

05:48.050 --> 05:49.580
A present?

05:51.520 --> 05:52.890
Is this it?

05:56.080 --> 05:58.250
I'm going to get revenge
on that woman!!

05:57.910 --> 05:59.210
Aki-sama.

05:59.580 --> 06:01.900
See you again next week!

05:59.880 --> 06:01.240
Aki-sama.

06:01.240 --> 06:02.800
Huh? What?

06:02.400 --> 06:06.630
<i>This program was brought to you
by the following sponsors.</i>

06:02.800 --> 06:05.340
The TV show is over.

06:05.340 --> 06:07.510
Huh? Oh...

06:08.050 --> 06:11.800
I guess there aren't many
interesting shows during New Year's.

06:11.800 --> 06:14.310
It's nothing but comedy shows and sports.

06:14.640 --> 06:17.120
Are you not going to go out anywhere?

06:17.120 --> 06:20.620
Where in the world am I going 
to go in this cold weather?

06:20.620 --> 06:22.060
You don't have any plans?

06:24.450 --> 06:27.140
No, not really.

06:28.280 --> 06:33.740
<b>January 4</b>

06:29.190 --> 06:33.210
It's not like I have any plans...

06:34.010 --> 06:36.270
Happy New Year!

06:36.270 --> 06:38.520
H-Happy New Year...

06:38.520 --> 06:41.580
Er, you guys sure have a lot 
of energy so early in the year.

06:41.980 --> 06:44.880
Well, the president and I were just talking.

06:45.180 --> 06:47.510
Talking? About what?

06:47.790 --> 06:50.190
We wanted to do our first 
shrine visit with everyone.

06:50.190 --> 06:52.590
Masamune-kun, did you already
do your first shrine visit?

06:52.590 --> 06:56.360
No, I just stayed at home for 
the first three days of the year.

06:56.360 --> 06:58.380
Then why don't we all go together?

06:58.380 --> 07:00.190
Huh? Right now?

07:01.570 --> 07:03.260
Okay, let's do it.

07:03.260 --> 07:04.770
Yay!

07:04.770 --> 07:07.950
Then let's go ahead and invite
Adagaki-san and the others, too.

07:07.950 --> 07:09.450
Just like when we went to the ocean!

07:09.450 --> 07:10.140
Huh?

07:15.510 --> 07:16.380
Well?

07:16.380 --> 07:19.660
E-Er, I mean, Adagaki-san seems busy,

07:19.660 --> 07:24.010
so I'm sure Master... Koiwai-san is, too.

07:24.010 --> 07:25.840
I see...

07:25.840 --> 07:29.720
Then let's at least see if
Fujinomiya-san is available.

07:43.990 --> 07:45.730
Come now, Neko-san.

07:45.730 --> 07:49.610
How am I supposed to move if 
you're holding onto me so tightly?

07:49.610 --> 07:51.700
You're so spooked by everything.

07:54.660 --> 07:56.400
Aw, how cute!

07:56.400 --> 07:59.310
She's probably around the 
same age as my Maa-kun.

07:59.310 --> 08:02.250
Oh, Maa-kun! Come here a second.

08:03.710 --> 08:06.170
Did you find the roast beef?!

08:07.520 --> 08:11.850
Maa-kun, say hi. This is 
Fujinomiya-san's daughter, Neko-chan.

08:11.850 --> 08:13.900
Aw, but where's the beef?

08:13.900 --> 08:15.390
Go on, Neko-chan.

08:33.610 --> 08:34.840
Want some?

08:35.900 --> 08:40.350
Come now, Masamune! You can't
just go putting food in your pockets!

08:40.350 --> 08:42.290
What? Did you want some, too, Dad?

08:42.290 --> 08:46.920
Oh, my. Maa-kun's pockets
are like a squirrel's cheeks!

08:57.680 --> 09:01.180
HNY! Masamune-kun, Kojuurou-kyun, 
and I are about to do our first shrine visit.
Did you want to come with us?

08:57.680 --> 09:01.180
Tae

09:01.640 --> 09:03.540
With Masamune-sama?

09:14.610 --> 09:16.780
Sorry to keep you waiting.

09:22.020 --> 09:24.650
Happy New Year.

09:24.650 --> 09:26.650
Happy New Year!

09:27.300 --> 09:30.410
I-I look forward to spending another 
year with you, Fujinomiya-san.

09:30.410 --> 09:33.090
Yes, likewise. To another year.

09:35.260 --> 09:39.160
I look forward to spending another year
with you, as well, Masamune-sama.

09:39.160 --> 09:40.440
Likewise.

09:42.050 --> 09:46.110
Um... Are Adagaki-san and 
Koiwai-san not joining us?

09:46.110 --> 09:48.150
Oh, uh, something came up...

09:50.610 --> 09:55.040
Okay! Onward to our first shrine visit!

09:55.040 --> 09:57.470
I'm gonna draw a great blessing in my fortune!

09:57.470 --> 09:58.820
Yeah!

09:59.300 --> 10:02.780
Now it just sounds like our motive
is to draw a great blessing.

10:16.630 --> 10:19.130
<b>Fortunes</b>

10:19.220 --> 10:21.090
<b>Luck</b>

10:19.220 --> 10:21.090
<b>Great Blessing</b>

10:23.220 --> 10:25.020
<b>Luck</b>

10:23.220 --> 10:25.020
<b>Mid Blessing</b>

10:27.140 --> 10:28.980
<b>Luck</b>

10:27.140 --> 10:28.980
<b>Future Blessing</b>

10:35.650 --> 10:37.610
<b>Chocolate Bananas</b>

10:37.610 --> 10:39.570
<b>Specialty Yakisoba</b>

10:38.280 --> 10:39.570
Step right up!

10:39.570 --> 10:41.930
How many you want? One? Two?

10:40.370 --> 10:43.030
What did you wish for, Masamune-kun?

10:41.930 --> 10:43.030
All right, one it is.

10:43.030 --> 10:44.970
What else?

10:43.390 --> 10:44.970
That'll be 500 yen.

10:44.970 --> 10:48.540
It must've been to be able to
have fun with Adagaki-san, right?

10:48.540 --> 10:51.940
Huh? Oh, yeah, something... like that.

10:55.340 --> 10:57.300
Oh! Hey, look!

10:57.500 --> 11:00.360
Hagoita! Hey! Let's play Hanetsuki!

11:00.360 --> 11:02.050
Sure, sounds fun!

11:02.050 --> 11:05.660
Oh, but Fujinomiya-san, do you think
you'll physically be able to play?

11:05.660 --> 11:08.590
Yes, a little exercise will be just fine.

11:08.590 --> 11:12.020
And this is quite nostalgic.

11:12.020 --> 11:16.980
<b>The Annual New Year
Fujinomiya Clan
Grand Hanetsuki
Tournament</b>

11:12.020 --> 11:18.280
The Annual New Year Fujinomiya Clan
Grand Hanetsuki Tournament!

11:16.210 --> 11:18.280
Back when I was little,

11:18.280 --> 11:21.660
everyone in my family, as well as
everyone who worked at our mansion,

11:21.660 --> 11:24.800
would have a grand hanetsuki tournament.

11:24.800 --> 11:27.420
Everyone in the Fujinomiya family?

11:27.420 --> 11:29.340
I can't even imagine.

11:30.640 --> 11:34.440
I think there's actually a park nearby.

11:37.870 --> 11:40.590
Well, it looks like the president
and I are on a team.

11:40.590 --> 11:42.750
The losing team has to buy everyone drinks.

11:42.750 --> 11:44.550
Bring it on.

11:45.090 --> 11:47.140
Okay, here we go.

11:47.680 --> 11:48.640
Hi-yah!

11:48.640 --> 11:49.710
Go!

11:49.710 --> 11:51.320
Whoa... There!

11:52.630 --> 11:53.600
Take that!

11:58.230 --> 12:00.500
Kojuurou-kyun!

12:00.500 --> 12:02.360
S-Sorry!

12:08.910 --> 12:11.750
Okay, now I'm gonna get serious!

12:14.170 --> 12:16.720
Kojuurou-kyun...

12:26.050 --> 12:29.630
Man, I'm pretty exhausted.

12:29.630 --> 12:32.770
Your face looks awful, Masamune-sama.

12:35.190 --> 12:37.190
Look who's talking, Fujinomiya-san.

12:42.370 --> 12:45.950
Man, I haven't laughed like this in a while.

12:45.950 --> 12:47.290
You haven't?

12:48.150 --> 12:50.070
Sorry to keep you waiting.

12:50.880 --> 12:54.650
Here. We lost, so this is on us.

12:54.650 --> 12:57.670
Were you okay with a 
sports drink, Masamune-kun?

12:57.980 --> 13:01.030
No, I'd prefer green tea,
since it helps with burning fat.

13:06.880 --> 13:08.760
See you later!

13:11.530 --> 13:13.450
Well, see you when the new term starts.

13:13.450 --> 13:14.680
See ya.

13:19.200 --> 13:22.600
Man, I think I had a bit too much fun.

13:25.680 --> 13:28.740
The hives are... gone?

13:35.590 --> 13:41.100
<i>I guess I ended up not seeing
Adagaki-san since Christmas Eve.</i>

13:41.100 --> 13:42.620
Hey, I think they're over there.

13:42.620 --> 13:43.380
Really?

14:25.010 --> 14:32.970
<b>Exam Room 1</b>

14:25.580 --> 14:27.950
Please come see me again in two weeks.

14:27.950 --> 14:30.310
I will. Thank you very much.

14:39.460 --> 14:41.020
Sorry to keep you waiting, Shidou.

14:41.500 --> 14:42.800
My lady.

14:42.800 --> 14:45.160
There were no issues. Let's go.

14:47.160 --> 14:48.950
Please go in, my lady.

14:49.970 --> 14:51.480
Fujinomiya-san!

14:54.060 --> 14:55.480
Masamune-sama...

14:55.950 --> 14:57.920
So I was right.

14:57.920 --> 15:02.190
I saw someone who looked like you in 
the lobby and thought it might be you.

15:02.190 --> 15:04.060
Are you here to visit someone?

15:04.060 --> 15:07.050
No, I'm here to get some test results.

15:07.520 --> 15:10.260
Oh, my. Are you not feeling well?

15:10.260 --> 15:13.850
Nah. There's nothing wrong at all.

15:13.850 --> 15:16.720
That's actually sorta the problem...

15:17.020 --> 15:19.400
Can we give you a ride?

15:19.400 --> 15:20.190
Huh?

15:20.600 --> 15:23.650
You can tell me all about it at my house.

15:26.340 --> 15:27.400
Here you are.

15:27.400 --> 15:29.320
Oh, um, th-thanks.

15:33.490 --> 15:37.330
<i>You'd better know what'll happen
if you do something to my lady.</i>

15:38.370 --> 15:40.790
<i>I'm not gonna do anything!</i>

15:40.790 --> 15:43.940
Sorry to keep you waiting, Masamune-sama.

15:46.690 --> 15:48.620
These are a gift from Kyoto.

15:48.620 --> 15:49.710
Thanks.

15:50.040 --> 15:53.430
So, is something troubling you?

15:54.820 --> 15:59.180
<i>The fact that I'm discussing
health issues with Fujinomiya Neko</i>

15:59.180 --> 16:01.370
<i>is a bit short-sighted, even for me.</i>

16:02.960 --> 16:06.400
Well... is there such a thing as

16:06.400 --> 16:10.120
stress affecting your body when there's 
technically nothing wrong with you?

16:11.890 --> 16:13.390
That's weird, right?

16:13.390 --> 16:14.990
If we're talking about stress...

16:15.450 --> 16:20.280
It should've been way worse when I was
hiding my origins and plotting my revenge...

16:21.620 --> 16:24.250
Is it because I still have
something I haven't said?

16:25.480 --> 16:29.620
But if I say that,
it'll affect Koiwai-san, too.

16:49.650 --> 16:50.840
Or perhaps...

16:50.840 --> 16:54.700
Maybe the cause is the fact that
you don't have a lie to tell anymore.

16:55.670 --> 16:58.620
I don't have a lie to tell?

16:59.570 --> 17:06.330
I have the perfect phrase to describe
you right now, Masamune-sama.

17:07.640 --> 17:09.040
And what's that?

17:13.220 --> 17:15.010
Burnout syndrome.

17:18.260 --> 17:22.720
Seeing your revenge through
was your reason to live.

17:22.720 --> 17:24.650
That was your lifelong wish.

17:25.050 --> 17:29.520
But that must mean that it having 
disappeared suddenly is still a shock to you,

17:29.520 --> 17:32.690
despite the fact that you're
going out with Aki-sama now.

17:33.940 --> 17:36.150
Because you don't actually love her.

17:37.320 --> 17:39.370
But... I...

17:39.370 --> 17:42.280
Used to love her back then?

17:46.150 --> 17:49.380
Is the past that important?

17:49.380 --> 17:50.750
Huh?

17:50.750 --> 17:56.090
I know this may not matter now,
but the truth is...

17:56.090 --> 17:58.760
I met you once before, a long time ago.

18:02.630 --> 18:05.980
Long before Aki-sama.

18:05.980 --> 18:07.050
Huh?

18:07.940 --> 18:09.940
Do you not remember?

18:10.440 --> 18:14.960
It was my relative Yuriko-neesan's wedding.

18:14.960 --> 18:20.410
Your family was invited due to
the groom's business relations.

18:20.410 --> 18:22.180
H-Huh?!

18:29.920 --> 18:31.130
Sorry!

18:31.130 --> 18:34.110
Even after all that, I don't remember it!

18:34.110 --> 18:36.970
I can't blame you for not remembering.

18:41.230 --> 18:44.520
I had half forgotten about it myself

18:44.520 --> 18:47.230
while I was wondering if I should 
have my surgery or not.

18:49.590 --> 18:52.730
Masamune-sama, do you remember
being here and saying,

18:52.730 --> 18:57.760
"You don't actually like me, either"?

18:57.760 --> 19:00.040
Well, yeah, of course...

19:04.680 --> 19:06.300
I remember that much...

19:08.310 --> 19:12.540
It frustrated me, but I couldn't argue.

19:12.540 --> 19:19.920
Because I was trying to start a game of love
just based on my meager memories.

19:20.560 --> 19:22.390
Fujinomiya-san...

19:22.840 --> 19:25.050
But you see, Masamune-sama...

19:25.050 --> 19:28.000
Even if my original intentions were dishonest,

19:28.000 --> 19:31.740
I'm not going to disparage
the person I've been since.

19:32.160 --> 19:33.100
Because...

19:35.640 --> 19:39.650
I can say this without any hesitation now.

19:40.160 --> 19:42.110
The past doesn't matter.

19:42.770 --> 19:46.260
I've fallen in love with you right now.

19:48.640 --> 19:50.470
What about you?

19:51.390 --> 19:56.750
I recommend casting aside your 
pretenses and preconceptions.

19:57.200 --> 20:00.630
So that you stop
blaming yourself, as well.

20:03.350 --> 20:09.970
Of course... I wouldn't mind
helping you with that if I can.

20:20.650 --> 20:22.110
Hold it right there!

20:22.110 --> 20:24.000
Please move, my lady!

20:24.000 --> 20:25.780
I'm going to extinguish this fool at once.

20:27.240 --> 20:30.300
Wha— Shidou-san! Calm down!

20:31.660 --> 20:34.670
There's nothing to worry about, Shidou.

20:41.950 --> 20:44.510
No mistakes will be happening here.

20:44.510 --> 20:46.550
Wait, this is...

20:46.970 --> 20:53.620
I think I'm also in need of casting aside
my pretenses and preconceptions.

20:58.180 --> 21:02.110
Masamune-sama, let me get 
you some more coffee.

21:15.710 --> 21:18.670
Messages

21:15.710 --> 21:18.670
Cruel Princess

21:15.710 --> 21:18.670
You went to the hospital, didn't you?
Was everything okay?

21:15.710 --> 21:18.670
Cruel Princess

21:22.950 --> 21:26.340
Pretenses and preconceptions, huh?

21:27.760 --> 21:31.110
<i>If there's a haze over my eyes right now...</i>

21:31.780 --> 21:34.470
<i>If there's some other truth...</i>

21:36.100 --> 21:39.450
Then I sure the hell would 
like to know what it is!

21:40.060 --> 21:40.860
Huh?!

21:41.440 --> 21:42.320
You okay?

21:42.320 --> 21:43.370
Come on, now.

21:43.370 --> 21:44.440
What's the matter?

21:44.840 --> 21:46.700
<i>Crap! Was that my fault?</i>

21:49.160 --> 21:51.740
I'm really sorry! Are you okay?

21:54.630 --> 21:56.020
Master?

21:58.170 --> 22:00.130
<b>Grapel</b>

22:07.360 --> 22:08.970
Pig's Foot...
